# Atlas frontend

## Architecture freeze (mandatory)

- Atlas Frontend Architecture **v1.0 is frozen** (M0–M3 proven). See architecture freeze in `apps/atlas-docs`.
- Do **not** change ownership boundaries, folder contracts, or shared extraction policy without explicit approval.
- Preserve: `chrome/` · `editorial/` · page-local `sections/` · typed `content/` fixtures.
- Forbidden without approval: page builders, section registries, dynamic-zone mappers, `packages/atlas-*`, speculative adapters.

## RSC-first (mandatory)

- Prefer React Server Components. Add `"use client"` only at the smallest necessary boundary.
- Avoid unnecessary client JS and global state. Do not add a state-management library unless React + local state are insufficient.
- Prefer accessible headless primitives for complex interactions; do not recreate focus/dialog/menu behavior from scratch without strong reason.
- Use semantic HTML, logical heading order, and proper image optimization.

## Rule of Two (mandatory)

Extract a shared component only when **at least two real production consumers** exist (or the Build Manifest names it a required publishing primitive).

- Page-local sections stay in `components/sections/` until a second route needs the same composition.
- Do not create generic cards, universal section APIs, or shared shells “for later.”

## Rule of Stability (mandatory)

A shared extract is allowed only when it **does not destabilize** frozen routes.

- If extracting would force visual or behavioral drift on Home / Work / Case Study (or other frozen pages), keep the composition local.
- Prefer revert over “almost shared.” Stability beats DRY.

## Fixture First (mandatory)

- Ship routes against typed fixtures in `src/content/` until approved Strapi mappers exist.
- Fixtures must mirror the planned CMS/domain shape so mappers target types — not reinvent props.
- Do not couple UI to live CMS before the mapping layer is ready.

## Domain model boundary (mandatory)

- UI consumes **normalized domain types** only — never raw Strapi/CMS DTOs.
- Keep transport shapes behind a data-access / mapping layer (prefer extending `@repo/strapi-client`).
- Domain types live in `content/` (or dedicated type modules), not inside fixture data files that sections import as “the model.”
- Production/CMS failures must degrade gracefully.

## Component structure (mandatory)

- Prefer explicit page and section components matching approved designs.
- Keep Atlas-specific UI in `apps/atlas-web`. Move to `packages/` only after genuine cross-app reuse.
- Keep components focused. Avoid overly generic prop APIs and deep abstraction layers.
- Reuse design tokens; do not invent values. Do not build components not required by an approved page design.

## Layout (guidance — frozen shape)

```text
apps/atlas-web/src/
├── app/
├── components/
│   ├── chrome/      # Nav, Footer, ReadingProgress
│   ├── editorial/   # Publishing primitives (Rule of Two)
│   └── sections/    # Page-local compositions
├── content/         # Domain types + fixtures
├── lib/
├── styles/
└── e2e/
```

Milestone completion gates live in `atlas-definition-of-done`. Design parity lives in `atlas-design`. Strapi tenancy lives in `atlas-strapi`.
